{
  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485), the dominant uncertainty is whether the image modality contributes any complementary signal beyond RNA. config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) is the minimal, most direct extension of config_001: it keeps the same RNA encoder and profile setting, and adds image with the simplest fusion (concat), isolating the effect of adding the image modality. If accuracy improves meaningfully over 0.485, we gain strong evidence to invest remaining budget in multimodal variants (better encoders, aggregation, fusion). If it does not improve, we can redirect budget toward RNA encoder or profile-setting improvements, avoiding a large block of potentially unproductive multimodal experiments. This single experiment resolves the highest-impact design question while changing the fewest variables from our existing data point."
}

